    "descricaoBreve": "Twenty-four. Became the Crime King of Marelia at eighteen. The rival who taught that some fights can't be won, only survived.",
    "descricaoCompleta": "Twenty-four years old. At eighteen he became the Crime King of Marelia, leader of organized crime across an entire region of the city. Alan didn't get where he is through inheritance or connections. He got there because he was the street kid nobody could break, and when the crime world realized that, it was only a matter of time. Security, enforcer, boss, boss of bosses. One step at a time, each earned the only way that world recognizes. Kim and Jack fought him for years. They lost. Came back. Lost again. Never won, but also never stopped, and Alan remembered that. When the duo's fame in LDI starts affecting his business, Alan doesn't act out of anger. He acts because visible weakness in a world like his has a price. The final encounter doesn't end in defeat or victory. It ends in a draw that both know means respect, and a deal: leave Marelia, preferably the country, and he guarantees protection for those left behind. He's not an antagonist. He's the rival who taught that some fights can't be won, only survived.",
